ine time-respecting cascade from 1017 to 1593 in [42136, 80535].", "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_16", "role": "confounder_control"}]}, "raw_final_response": "```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_85c5e4e7\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [1017, 1593],\n  \"window\": [42136, 80535],\n  \"confidence\": 0.6,\n  \"narrative\": \"No direct 1017->1593 edge exists at any time (step_15), so any cascade must be multi-hop. 1017 has 25 events / 25 distinct partners and 1593 has 23 events / 23 partners (step_02) - both are low-activity, near-tree nodes with almost no repeat structure (global repeat_ratio 0.054, step_01), so there is little opportunity for tightly spaced relay events. Enumerating 1017's out-neighbourhood (25, 65, 160, 1314, 949, 1866, ... step_03) and 1593's in-neighbourhood (26, 64, 478, 502, 603, 706, 830, 873, 961, 971, 1000, 1215, 1325, 1477, 1529, 1622, 1631, 1870, 1916, 1940; step_04) shows the two sets are disjoint, and the second-hop out-sets of 1017's successors (steps 08-13) contain none of 1593's in-neighbours either. Hence even with time ignored, the shortest directed route is 4+ hops and runs through the global super-hubs (158, 1726, 639, 698, 319, 595; step_07, and the 2-hop expansions in step_0